    "ucrCourseEvidence": "The assembled programme was reviewed against systematic theology, eight Biblical Greek and Hebrew courses and exegesis in the biblical languages. World Myth & Literature compares narratives across cultures, art and archaeology study material evidence, and Ethics examines moral arguments. These courses make substantive contributions to the study of religion in culture. They do not develop Christian doctrine or the interpretation of biblical texts as sustained subjects. Technology and health ethics likewise concern applied moral reasoning.",
